SPL Example:
index=web status!=200 
| stats count by status, uri 
| sort -count 
| head 10

This finds the top 10 URIs returning non-200 HTTP status codes.

Common Use Cases
Troubleshooting outages by correlating logs across services
Detecting security breaches via behavioral analytics
Compliance auditing (PCI-DSS, HIPAA, GDPR)
Business analytics from clickstream or IoT data
DevOps observability with distributed tracing


Strengths & Considerations
Strengths: Extremely flexible data ingestion, powerful SPL, massive ecosystem of apps, strong security focus.
Considerations: Licensing is volume-based (per GB indexed), which can get expensive at scale. Query performance depends heavily on indexing strategy and hardware.


